<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mwezi IV Gisabo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1840–<a href="/years/1908">1908</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mwezi IV Gisabo was mwami (king) of Burundi from about 1852 to 1908, the last to rule before effective colonial control. He fought off Swahili-Arab slave traders and rival princes, and for years resisted German forces from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-east-africa">German East Africa</a>. In 1903 he accepted German overlordship by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kiganda">Treaty of Kiganda</a>, keeping his throne under colonial rule until his death.</p></div>
